; MX3 (part 3) the 0F page (docs/v35s-mechanisms.md section 3.4; README "MX3 (part 3)").
; The E word pops the second opcode byte with the 0F opcode (into the ModR/M register, as a
; ModR/M form's E word pops its ModR/M byte: the frozen model's start takes the page's second
; byte, page_take=own) and the dispatch reads the second level on it (the decode's op3: the
; second byte's bits 3:1, the operation; w: the operand width). A form with a ModR/M byte pops
; it on its routine's first word, an EAC word: its mode decides the next word (register mode:
; the label, the register form's path; a memory mode: the EA head of the mode called, returning
; to the memory path's add; mod 00 without a head: the add). Every routine is the data book's
; formula first; a clock beyond it is a named act or an OPEN word declared "silicon longer than
; the book" with the run the frozen model is exact on. Clocks in the comments are from the E
; word that popped the 0F opcode (E + 0; the dispatch E + 1; the routine's first word E + 2).

; ---- the packed BCD strings: ADD4S / SUB4S (0F 20 / 22), CMP4S (0F 26). (CL + 1) / 2 byte
; pairs; the source byte at DS0:IX + i (a prefix's segment), read before the destination's at
; DS1:IY + i, the result written back (ADD4S / SUB4S). The loop counter is loaded by the first
; word from CL (CN_CLH: CL shifted right by one with its low bit as the carry-in); a zero count
; skips the loop. tmpc is the pair's offset i. Every request is posted with its address already
; in the address register; the destination's address moves on the source read's second clock
; (before any wait state: MX1g's BW law would hold a move under a wait state), the next pair's
; after the write's end. F after the write: the EU holds until the write's end (RAMEN = 1, the
; write may land in the registers' RAM: mechanisms 3.3).

routine add4s op=20,22 page=0f book="ADD4S" n=4 diff=1 why="OPEN: silicon longer than the book by one (F32-push-add4s-n4-k1-pE-w0: the frozen model exact; the start at +87 on the fetch's grant, the source read issued at +104 (E + 17), the destination's at done + 6, the write at done + 9, the next pair's source at the write's end + 6, the next start at the last write's end + 12: 83 clocks for two pairs against the book's 82; F32-out-add4s-n2-k2-pE-w0 53 for one pair, F32-out-add4s-n4-k1-pE-w2 the same clocks with the bus cycles' waits and the source read's setup + 2: the address move under the start's fetch's wait states, MX1g's BW law); per pair the book's 30 (three bus cycles, the BCD step, the address moves and the book's clocks with no act, OPEN); the fixed part the book's 22 + 1"
    ra=IX rb=CW wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA d2=TC s2=ZERO cnt=CLH alu=BCDI ; the source's address (IX + 0), the pair offset 0 into tmpc, the counter <- (CL + 1) / 2; the carry cleared, the zero term set (E + 2: the move waits out the start's fetch's wait states, MX1g's BW law)
    open                                    ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (ADD4S 22 + 30n)
    jc=CNTZ:a4_tail                         ; no byte pair: the flags
    open call=w10                           ; OPEN: 11 clocks: a book clock with no act (ADD4S 22 + 30n) (the call and the shared delay's 10)
a4_pair: bus=MEMR seg=DSP wid=BYTE          ; post the source byte's read (E + 16: it issues at E + 17, the model's)
    ra=IY wid=WORD alu=ADD ax=RA ay=TC      ; SIGMA = IY + i
    d1=ADDR s1=SIG                          ; the destination's address (the read's second clock: no wait state yet)
    alu=ADD ax=TC ay=ONE                    ; SIGMA = i + 1
    f d1=TA s1=OPR d2=TC s2=SIG             ; F: the source byte into tmpa; tmpc <- i + 1 (the read's end)
    open call=w3                            ; OPEN: 4 clocks: a book clock with no act (ADD4S 30 a pair) (the call and the shared delay's 3)
    bus=MEMR seg=DS1 wid=BYTE               ; post the destination byte's read (the source's end + 5: issued at + 6, the model's)
    f d1=TB s1=OPR                          ; F: the destination byte into tmpb (the read's end)
    alu=BCDS ax=TB ay=TA wid=BYTE           ; the BCD byte step (the add / the subtract by op3; the carry in and out, the zero term)
    d1=OPRW s1=SIG                          ; the result into the write datum
    open call=w4                            ; OPEN: 5 clocks: a book clock with no act (ADD4S 30 a pair) (the call and the shared delay's 4)
    bus=MEMW seg=DS1 wid=BYTE               ; post the write (the destination's end + 8: issued at + 9, the model's)
    f                                       ; F: the write's end (the RAMEN hold)
    ra=IX wid=WORD alu=ADD ax=RA ay=TC      ; SIGMA = IX + i (the next pair)
    d1=ADDR s1=SIG                          ; the next source's address
    open                                    ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (ADD4S 30 a pair)
    loop=a4_pair                            ; the counter step: the next pair (its post at the write's end + 5)
a4_tail: open call=w5                       ; OPEN: 6 clocks: a book clock with no act (ADD4S 22 + 30n) (the call and the shared delay's 5)
    alu=BCDF wf                             ; the flags: CY S AC the last carry, Z P the zero term, V 0
    e wb                                    ; E: pop the next opcode (the last write's end + 12, the model's next start); the flags' write-back runs on past E (the model's wb 2: an OUT imm8 after it waits, MX1f)

routine cmp4s op=26 page=0f book="CMP4S" n=4 diff=2 why="OPEN: silicon longer than the book by two (F32-out-cmp4s-n4-k1-pE-w0: the frozen model exact; the source read issued at E + 17, the destination's at the source's end + 6, the next pair's source at the destination's end + 13, the next start at the last destination's end + 20: 74 for two pairs against the book's 72; F32-out-cmp4s-n2-k2-pE-w1 the same with the waits and the BW law's clock); per pair the book's 25 (two bus cycles, the BCD step, the address moves, OPEN clocks); the fixed part the book's 22 + 2"
    ra=IX rb=CW wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA d2=TC s2=ZERO cnt=CLH alu=BCDI ; the source's address (IX + 0), the pair offset 0 into tmpc, the counter <- (CL + 1) / 2; the borrow cleared, the zero term set (E + 2: the BW law)
    open                                    ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (CMP4S 22 + 25n)
    jc=CNTZ:c4_tail                         ; no byte pair: the flags
    open call=w10                           ; OPEN: 11 clocks: a book clock with no act (CMP4S 22 + 25n) (the call and the shared delay's 10)
c4_pair: bus=MEMR seg=DSP wid=BYTE          ; post the source byte's read (E + 16: issued at E + 17)
    ra=IY wid=WORD alu=ADD ax=RA ay=TC      ; SIGMA = IY + i
    d1=ADDR s1=SIG                          ; the destination's address (the read's second clock)
    alu=ADD ax=TC ay=ONE                    ; SIGMA = i + 1
    f d1=TA s1=OPR d2=TC s2=SIG             ; F: the source byte into tmpa; tmpc <- i + 1
    open call=w3                            ; OPEN: 4 clocks: a book clock with no act (CMP4S 25 a pair) (the call and the shared delay's 3)
    bus=MEMR seg=DS1 wid=BYTE               ; post the destination byte's read (the source's end + 5)
    f d1=TB s1=OPR                          ; F: the destination byte into tmpb
    alu=BCDS ax=TB ay=TA wid=BYTE           ; the BCD byte step (the subtract: the borrow and the zero term; nothing written)
    ra=IX wid=WORD alu=ADD ax=RA ay=TC      ; SIGMA = IX + i (the next pair)
    d1=ADDR s1=SIG                          ; the next source's address
    open call=w6                            ; OPEN: 7 clocks: a book clock with no act (CMP4S 25 a pair) (the call and the shared delay's 6)
    loop=c4_pair                            ; the counter step: the next pair (its post at the destination's end + 12)
c4_tail: open call=w6                       ; OPEN: 7 clocks: a book clock with no act (CMP4S 22 + 25n) (the call and the shared delay's 6)
    alu=BCDF wf                             ; the flags
    e wb                                    ; E: pop the next opcode (the last destination's end + 20, the model's next start); the flags' write-back past E (the model's wb 2, MX1f)

; ---- the bit operations TEST1 / CLR1 / SET1 / NOT1 (0F 10-1F: op3 1:0 the operation, the
; width the second byte's bit 0, bit 3 an imm3 / imm4 index after the operand, else CL; the
; index modulo the width). The first word pops the ModR/M byte (EAC): a register operand goes
; to the register path (the operand and CL read on ports B and A, the bit operation, the write);
; a memory operand calls the EA head of its mode and returns to the add, the read, F with the
; bit operation, the write's post, E held to its end (RAMEN). The CL index is read into tmpb
; after the add; the imm index is popped after the read's issue (the frozen model's takes).
routine b1tcl op=10,11 page=0f diff=r:-1,m00:+0,d8:+0,d16:+0,dir:+0 book="TEST1 reg8,CL" bookm="TEST1 mem8,CL" why="OPEN: the book's TEST1 reg,CL 7 / mem,CL EA + 12, the book's clocks with no act OPEN; the memory paths one over the book's EA: the ModR/M byte's pop on a word of its own (the EAC word, a pop the book's EA does not count: the E word pops only the page's second byte), the frozen model exact on F32-push-test1_mw_cl-k1-pE-w0 and F32-push-set1_mw_cl-k1-pE-w0 (16 and 19 S-to-S at mod 00); book error: silicon's clocks are the routine's words and the take sync's wait (the ModR/M pop arms it: the register path's operation and the memory path's add wait for the fetch the pop's room asked for, MX1f / Correction 15; the book machine has no sync), F32-out-set1_rw_cl-k1-pE-w0 and F34-push-rbit-set1_rw_cl-l0-k1-pE-w0 (9 S-to-S each)"
    pop=modrm eac=b1tcl_r                   ; pop the ModR/M byte (E + 2): register mode to the register path; a memory mode calls its EA head
    ea=BI ra=BASE rb=INDEX resv             ; the EA's add into the address register; the reservation
    ra=CW d1=TB s1=RA                       ; CL (by the width) into tmpb: the bit index
    open                                    ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (TEST1 mem,CL EA + 12)
    open                                    ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (TEST1 mem,CL EA + 12)
    bus=MEMR                                ; post the read (E + 10 with the take sync's wait at the add: issued at E + 11, the model's)
    f alu=BIT ax=OPR ay=TB wf               ; F: TEST1 on the datum at the bit CL names (S Z P; CY AC V cleared)
    open                                    ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (TEST1 mem,CL EA + 12)
    e                                       ; E: pop the next opcode (TEST1 writes nothing)
b1tcl_r: open                              ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (TEST1 reg,CL 7) (the take sync's wait first)
    open                                    ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (TEST1 reg,CL 7)
    open                                    ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (TEST1 reg,CL 7)
    e                                       ; E: pop the next opcode
    ra=CW rb=RM alu=BIT ax=RB ay=RA wf      ; the word after E: the register and CL, TEST1's flags written (the write port's: MX3's WBR)

routine b1tim op=18,19 page=0f diff=r:0,m00:+0,d8:+0,d16:+0,dir:+0 book="TEST1 reg8,imm3" bookm="TEST1 mem8,imm3" why="OPEN: the book's TEST1 reg,imm 6 / mem,imm EA + 9, the book's clocks with no act OPEN; the index popped after the read's issue (the frozen model's take)"
    pop=modrm eac=b1tim_r                   ; pop the ModR/M byte (E + 2)
    ea=BI ra=BASE rb=INDEX resv             ; the EA's add; the reservation
    bus=MEMR                                ; post the read (E + 7 with the take sync's wait at the add: issued at E + 8, the model's)
    open                                    ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (TEST1 mem,imm EA + 9)
    pop=il                                  ; pop the bit index (the clock after the read's issue: the model's take)
    f alu=BIT ax=OPR ay=IMM8 wf             ; F: TEST1 on the datum at the bit the index names
    open                                    ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (TEST1 mem,imm EA + 9)
    e                                       ; E: pop the next opcode
b1tim_r: pop=il                             ; pop the bit index
    open d1=TB s1=IMM8                      ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (TEST1 reg,imm 6) (the take sync's wait first); (F5c) the index into tmpb (the next E pop's short displacement overwrites IL before the word after E: f5c_084 TEST1 IX, 60h / DBNZNE)
    open                                    ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (TEST1 reg,imm 6)
    e                                       ; E: pop the next opcode
    rb=RM alu=BIT ax=RB ay=TB wf            ; the word after E: the register and the index (tmpb), TEST1's flags written (the write port's: MX3's WBR)

routine b1ccl op=12,13 page=0f diff=r:-2,m00:+0,d8:+0,d16:+0,dir:+0 book="CLR1 reg8,CL" bookm="CLR1 mem8,CL" why="OPEN: the book's CLR1 reg,CL 8 / mem,CL EA + 16, the book's clocks with no act OPEN; the memory paths one over the book's EA: the ModR/M byte's pop on a word of its own (the EAC word, a pop the book's EA does not count: the E word pops only the page's second byte), the frozen model exact on F32-push-test1_mw_cl-k1-pE-w0 and F32-push-set1_mw_cl-k1-pE-w0 (16 and 19 S-to-S at mod 00); book error: silicon's clocks are the routine's words and the take sync's wait (the ModR/M pop arms it: the register path's operation and the memory path's add wait for the fetch the pop's room asked for, MX1f / Correction 15; the book machine has no sync), F32-out-set1_rw_cl-k1-pE-w0 and F34-push-rbit-set1_rw_cl-l0-k1-pE-w0 (9 S-to-S each)"
    pop=modrm eac=b1ccl_r                   ; pop the ModR/M byte (E + 2)
    ea=BI ra=BASE rb=INDEX resv             ; the EA's add; the reservation
    ra=CW d1=TB s1=RA                       ; CL into tmpb: the bit index
    open                                    ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (CLR1 mem,CL EA + 16)
    open                                    ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (CLR1 mem,CL EA + 16)
    bus=MEMR                                ; post the read (E + 10 with the take sync's wait at the add: issued at E + 11, the model's)
    f alu=BIT ax=OPR ay=TB resv             ; F: CLR1 on the datum; the reservation
    open                                    ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (CLR1 mem,CL EA + 16)
    d1=OPRW s1=SIG bus=MEMW                 ; the result into the write datum; post the write
    e                                       ; E: held until the write's end (RAMEN)
b1ccl_r: open                              ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (CLR1 reg,CL 8) (the take sync's wait first)
    open                                    ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (CLR1 reg,CL 8)
    open                                    ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (CLR1 reg,CL 8)
    ra=CW rb=RM alu=BIT ax=RB ay=RA e       ; the register and CL: CLR1; E (the E row's operation, a register form's)
    wr=RM ws=SIG                            ; the register written on the word after E (its write port: MX3's WBR)

routine b1cim op=1A,1B page=0f diff=r:-1,m00:+0,d8:+0,d16:+0,dir:+0 book="CLR1 reg8,imm3" bookm="CLR1 mem8,imm3" why="OPEN: the book's CLR1 reg,imm 7 / mem,imm EA + 13, the book's clocks with no act OPEN; the index popped after the read's issue; the memory paths one over the book's EA: the ModR/M byte's pop on a word of its own (the EAC word, a pop the book's EA does not count), the frozen model exact on F32-push-not1_mb_imm-k1-pE-w0 (16 S-to-S at mod 00); book error: silicon's clocks are the routine's words and the take sync's wait (MX1f / Correction 15: the book machine has no sync), F32-out-set1_rw_imm-k1-pE-w0 (9 S-to-S)"
    pop=modrm eac=b1cim_r                   ; pop the ModR/M byte (E + 2)
